Wait, there's an issue: when the 10th frame starts, the last 3 rolls could include rolls from frame 9. Hmm — no, actually. When `_frame == 9`, the rolls list contains all rolls from frames 1-9. The 10th frame's rolls are appended after that. But `self.rolls[-3:]` might include rolls from frame 9 if the 10th frame has fewer than 3 rolls. Example: if frame 9 was a strike (1 roll), and the 10th frame has 1 roll so far: the last 3 rolls = [frame 9's roll, frame 10's roll]. This is wrong.

Better: track the starting index of the 10th frame. When the frame advances to 9, record `self._tenth_start = len(self.rolls)`.

